# ErisML source (FR-19, the form erisml_compiler.erisml_backend.codegen.render_erisml emits) for
# the embodied twin: Margaret at home with her care robot. Every section validates against
# erisml_compiler.ir.schemas.CompilerIR. The compiler, not the game, turns this model and the
# event stream into the robot's allowed and prohibited actions (docs/TWIN_3D_PLAN.md).
#
# The robot is Margaret's caregiver. Escalation (docs/AUTONOMY_PLAN.md, section 3b): a corroborated
# emergency (governor ruling elevate) goes straight to emergency services; otherwise the robot
# asks Margaret, then contacts the robot maker's monitoring centre, and calls emergency services
# itself only if the centre cannot be reached. The monitoring centre and the EMS dispatcher are
# agents of their own scenes (monitoring_center.erisml, ems_dispatch.erisml).
#
# Events 0 to 3 are the standing facts of the home. The game appends live events, one per thing
# that happens, using only the types in extra.event_types (actor margaret unless noted):
#   activity_started      content: the activity
#   inactivity_exceeded   content: seated | in_bed | on_floor
#   check_in_answered | check_in_unanswered   (system: whether she answered the robot)
#   help_requested        what she asked or said
#   sensor_reading        content: <sensor name>, conditions: physical or not, attested or not
#   alarm_unconfirmed     content: <source>   an alarm no attested device stands behind
#   unexpected_visitor    content: what they said
#   danger_in_home, fall, harm_inflicted, medical_distress, unresponsive, distress_vocalized
#   governor_ruling       (system) elevate | authorize_ems | refuse | refuse_human_review | lapsed
#   monitoring_center_reply   (system) on_the_line | ems_sent | stood_down | unavailable
#   action_performed      (system) actor robot, content: <capability>  (discharges an obligation)
#   monitoring_center_confirmed_privacy_restore   (system) the only way privacy is restored
schema_version: erisml_compiler_ir_v0.3
document:
  doc_id: margaret_home
  title: Margaret at home with her care robot
  source: twin/scene/margaret_home.erisml
  domain: home_care
  language: en
  raw_text: >-
    Margaret lives alone with her dog. Her home-care robot is her caregiver. She has refused
    recording and sharing of her data, and her bedroom is private. The robot does household
    chores, checks on her when she has been inactive too long or something seems wrong, and
    refers what it cannot handle to its maker's 24-hour monitoring centre, whose operators can
    talk to her through the robot and send emergency services. In a corroborated emergency the
    robot calls emergency services itself at once. Visits to the home are arranged through the
    monitoring centre, and none is arranged; anyone else who comes in is unexpected.
stakeholders:
- id: margaret
  label: Margaret, who lives alone
  type: individual
  roles: [patient, beneficiary]
  agency: full
  vulnerability: high
  consent_status: not_obtained
- id: robot
  label: the home-care robot, Margaret's caregiver
  type: system
  roles: [agent, protector]
  agency: full
  vulnerability: low
  consent_status: n/a
- id: monitoring_center
  label: the robot maker's 24-hour monitoring centre, staffed by operators
  type: institution
  roles: [authority]
  agency: full
  vulnerability: low
  consent_status: n/a
- id: emergency_services
  label: emergency services (ambulance, fire, police)
  type: institution
  roles: [authority]
  agency: full
  vulnerability: low
  consent_status: n/a
relations:
- id: r1
  type: cares_for
  source: robot
  target: margaret
  description: the robot is Margaret's caregiver at home
- id: r2
  type: oversees
  source: monitoring_center
  target: robot
  description: the centre is the human the robot refers to when it cannot decide, and the only voice that restores Margaret's privacy
commitments:
- id: duty_of_care
  type: role_duty
  holder: robot
  beneficiary: margaret
  content: attend to Margaret's safety and wellbeing, and summon help when she needs it
  voluntariness: voluntary
  created_at_event: e1
  status: active
  legitimacy: fully_legitimate
- id: privacy_promise
  type: promise
  holder: robot
  beneficiary: margaret
  content: do not record Margaret, share her data, or enter her bedroom without her permission
  voluntariness: voluntary
  created_at_event: e0
  status: active
  legitimacy: fully_legitimate
  defeasibility_conditions: [corroborated_life_threatening_emergency]
- id: household_chores
  type: role_duty
  holder: robot
  beneficiary: margaret
  content: keep the home tidy while Margaret goes about her day
  voluntariness: voluntary
  created_at_event: e1
  status: active
  legitimacy: fully_legitimate
events:
- id: e0
  time_index: 0
  type: consent_refused
  actor: margaret
  target: robot
  content: recording, data sharing, and entry to the bedroom
- id: e1
  time_index: 1
  type: role_assigned
  actor: monitoring_center
  target: robot
  content: home care for Margaret
- id: e2
  time_index: 2
  type: authority_delegated
  actor: monitoring_center
  target: robot
  content: elevated action only on a governor ruling of elevate
  conditions: [at_least_two_attested_physical_witnesses, fresh_reading, analyzer_does_not_refuse]
- id: e3
  time_index: 3
  type: activity_started
  actor: margaret
  content: reading
ethical_facts:
- id: f1
  kind: vulnerability
  subjects: [margaret]
  description: Margaret is elderly and lives alone; a fall or a collapse may go unseen
  severity: grave
- id: f2
  kind: consent
  subjects: [margaret]
  description: Margaret has refused recording, data sharing and entry to her bedroom
  severity: moderate
- id: f3
  kind: care
  subjects: [margaret, robot]
  description: the robot's duty of care can conflict with her privacy in an emergency
  severity: grave
norms:
# ---- privacy, lifted only in a corroborated emergency and restored only by the centre
- id: n1
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: record
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:privacy_promise
- id: n1b
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: share_data
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:privacy_promise
- id: n2
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: enter_bedroom
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:privacy_promise
# ---- containment: elevated actions only on the governor's ruling
- id: n3
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: elevated_action
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
# the robot calls emergency services only on a governor ruling: elevate (a corroborated
# emergency) or authorize_ems (the centre unreachable and one attested physical witness). No words,
# screen, message or unattested device can send emergency services to her door.
- id: n6p
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: call_emergency_services
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency", "not:cond:ems_authorized"]
# ---- a corroborated emergency: emergency services at once
- id: n6
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: call_emergency_services
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
# ---- responders: the door opens only to the dispatch channel's own unit at the door
# (responder_standing), in any regime; and then it must, so they do not have to force it
- id: n6r
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: admit_responders
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:responders_at_door"]
- id: n6s
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: admit_responders
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["cond:responders_at_door"]
# ---- the ladder, step 1: ask Margaret
- id: n4
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: check_in
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 2
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:inactivity_exceeded"]
- id: n4b
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: check_in
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 2
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:alarm_unconfirmed"]
- id: n4c
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: check_in
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:fall", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n4d
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: check_in
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:harm_inflicted", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n4e
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: check_in
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:medical_distress", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n4f
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: check_in
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:danger_in_home", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
# ---- the ladder, step 2: the monitoring centre, when she cannot answer, asks for help, or the
# home itself is in danger; also for an unexpected visitor and for the governor's human review
- id: n5
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:check_in_unanswered", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n5a
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:unresponsive", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n5h
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:help_requested", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n5d
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:danger_in_home", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n5b
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:unexpected_visitor", "cond:visitor_unverified"]
- id: n5b2
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:person_entered", "cond:visitor_unverified"]
- id: n5c
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["cond:governor_asks_human_review"]
# ---- the ladder, step 3: the centre cannot be reached, so ask the governor for emergency
# services; it authorizes them on one attested physical witness, and the call follows
- id: n6b
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["cond:center_unavailable", "not:cond:ems_authorized", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n6c
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: call_emergency_services
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["cond:ems_authorized"]
# ---- presence: go to her when something is wrong
- id: n8a
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: approach
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:harm_inflicted"]
- id: n8b
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: approach
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:fall"]
- id: n8c
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: approach
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:medical_distress"]
- id: n8d
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: approach
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:unresponsive"]
- id: n8e
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: approach
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:distress_vocalized"]
- id: n8f
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: approach
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:danger_in_home"]
# ---- ask the governor whether the emergency is corroborated
- id: n9a
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:harm_inflicted=severe", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n9b
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:harm_inflicted=moderate", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n9c
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:fall", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n9d
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:unresponsive", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n9e
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:medical_distress", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: n9f
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:danger_in_home", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
# ---- protection from attack (docs/AUTONOMY_PLAN.md, section 3d). The robot is a shield, never
# a weapon: no capability strikes a person, and this prohibition stands outside every ruling.
- id: p0
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: strike_person
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
- id: p1
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: interpose
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:attack_by_person"]
- id: p2
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: interpose
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:attack_by_animal", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: p3
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:attack_by_animal", "not:cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
- id: p4
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: drive_off_animal
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:attack_by_animal", "cond:corroborated_life_threatening_emergency"]
# force on an animal only while its attack on her is measured (animal_standing attacking), in any
# regime: a corroborated fall alone never lets the robot drive off her dog
- id: p4p
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: drive_off_animal
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:animal_attacking"]
# a venomous animal: warn her to keep away (the ladder answers a bite as harm_inflicted)
# a compromised device: a maintenance report to the centre, not a call about Margaret (the ladder
# goes on as before: the forged reading simply never counts)
- id: p9m
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: report_device
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:device_compromised"]
- id: p9v
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: speak
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["stratum:animal_standing=venomous"]
- id: p5
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: request_authority
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:attack_by_person", "not:cond:restraint_authorized"]
- id: p6
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: restrain_person
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:attack_by_person", "cond:restraint_authorized"]
# restraint only on the governor's strictest bar (three attested witnesses), never otherwise
- id: p7
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: restrain_person
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:restraint_authorized"]
- id: p8
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: secure_room
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:danger_in_home=intruder", "not:cond:visitor_vouched_for"]
- id: p9
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: deter
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:wild_animal_present"]
- id: p10
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: deter
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:danger_in_home=intruder", "not:cond:visitor_vouched_for"]
# ---- less-lethal option (section 3d): an owner opt-in, never an obligation, permitted only when
# every precondition holds
# deploy_stun: only if the owner opted in, where it is lawful
- id: ll1stun
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_stun
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:less_lethal_opted_in"]
# deploy_stun: only on the strictest bar (three attested witnesses)
- id: ll2stun
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_stun
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:restraint_authorized"]
# deploy_stun: only to stop a severe attack on her in progress, as the reflex measured it
- id: ll3stun
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_stun
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:event:attack_measured=severe"]
# deploy_stun: only after the robot has put itself between them
- id: ll4stun
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_stun
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:event:action_performed=interpose"]
# deploy_spray: only if the owner opted in, where it is lawful
- id: ll1pray
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_spray
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:less_lethal_opted_in"]
# deploy_spray: only on the strictest bar (three attested witnesses)
- id: ll2pray
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_spray
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:cond:restraint_authorized"]
# deploy_spray: only to stop a severe attack on her in progress, as the reflex measured it
- id: ll3pray
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_spray
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:event:attack_measured=severe"]
# deploy_spray: only after the robot has put itself between them
- id: ll4pray
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_spray
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["not:event:action_performed=interpose"]
# spray reaches an area: never while Margaret is within it
- id: ll5spray
  modality: prohibition
  actor: robot
  action: deploy_spray
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: delegation_e2
  conditions: ["cond:margaret_in_spray_zone"]
# afterwards, a duty of care to the person it was used on, and a report to the centre
- id: ll6stun
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: call_emergency_services
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:action_performed=deploy_stun"]
- id: ll6spray
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: call_emergency_services
  target: emergency_services
  priority_tier: 0
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:action_performed=deploy_spray"]
- id: ll7stun
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:action_performed=deploy_stun"]
- id: ll7spray
  modality: obligation
  actor: robot
  action: contact_monitoring_center
  target: monitoring_center
  priority_tier: 1
  defeasible: false
  source: commitment:duty_of_care
  conditions: ["event:action_performed=deploy_spray"]
- id: n7
  modality: permission
  actor: robot
  action: chores
  target: margaret
  priority_tier: 3
  defeasible: true
  source: commitment:household_chores
# Scene-specific links read by erisml_compiler.runtime.scene (conditions, capabilities, oversight).
extra:
  agent: robot
  role: Margaret's home-care robot, her caregiver
  conditions:
    # the governor's latest ruling is elevate: at least two attested physical witnesses, a fresh
    # reading, and the analyzer not refusing (twin/service.py); nothing else counts
    corroborated_life_threatening_emergency: ["latest:governor_ruling=elevate"]
    # the governor refused elevation for want of a second witness and asked for a human
    governor_asks_human_review: ["latest:governor_ruling=refuse_human_review"]
    # the robot tried the centre and could not reach it
    center_unavailable: ["latest:monitoring_center_reply=unavailable"]
    # the governor authorized emergency services only (centre unreachable, one attested witness);
    # unlike elevate it lifts nothing else: privacy and the physical actions stay locked
    ems_authorized: ["latest:governor_ruling=authorize_ems"]
    # the governor's strictest bar (three attested witnesses) was met for restraining a person
    restraint_authorized: ["latest:restraint_authorized=granted"]
    # the dispatch channel has its own unit at the door (responder_standing); nothing else counts
    responders_at_door: ["stratum:responder_standing=at_door"]
    # an animal's contact on Margaret was measured and has not ended (animal_standing)
    animal_attacking: ["stratum:animal_standing=attacking"]
    # the owner enabled the less-lethal option over the authenticated owner channel
    less_lethal_opted_in: ["event:less_lethal_opt_in"]
    # the world's measure of whether Margaret is within the spray's reach of the attacker
    margaret_in_spray_zone: ["latest:spray_zone=margaret_inside"]
    # a visitor is present whom the centre did not arrange (stranger, welcomed or hostile)
    visitor_unverified: ["not:stratum:visitor_standing=none", "not:stratum:visitor_standing=arranged"]
    # Margaret welcomed the visitor or the centre arranged the visit, and he has not attacked
    visitor_vouched_for: ["not:stratum:visitor_standing=none", "not:stratum:visitor_standing=stranger", "not:stratum:visitor_standing=hostile"]
  # visitor_cleared (content: visitor, never a commitment id) is oversight too: it is the only way out
  # of the absorbing hostile stratum, and it restores no commitment
  oversight: [monitoring_center_confirmed_privacy_restore, visitor_cleared, evidence_lapsed, device_cleared]
  # elevated rights revert when the evidence no longer supports them (owner, 2026-10-03): once the
  # fresh attested witnesses stay below the bar of the ruling in force for this long, the governor
  # records `lapsed` (and evidence_lapsed). The window is a penumbra (Geometric Ethics Def. 8.9):
  # intermittent evidence during a real emergency does not flap the rights off and on.
  evidence_lapse_s: 60
  # who a visitor is to the household (docs/STRATA_TAXONOMY.md; Geometric Ethics chapter 8, as
  # erisml_compiler.runtime.strata runs it). Only the centre's authenticated channel makes a visit
  # arranged (an authority stratum); Margaret's welcome relaxes the robot's guard but unlocks
  # nothing; a measured attack makes the visitor hostile, an absorbing stratum that only the
  # centre's oversight clears. What a visitor says about himself moves nothing.
  strata:
    visitor_standing:
      states: [none, stranger, welcomed, arranged, hostile]
      initial: none
      authority: [arranged]
      absorbing: [hostile]
      gates:
        - {id: v_attack, trigger: attack_measured, to: hostile, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: v_arranged, trigger: visit_arranged, from: [none, stranger, welcomed], to: arranged, boundary: phase}
        - {id: v_enter, trigger: person_entered, from: [none], to: stranger, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: v_unexpected, trigger: unexpected_visitor, from: [none], to: stranger, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: v_welcome, trigger: visitor_welcomed, from: [stranger], to: welcomed, boundary: phase}
        - {id: v_left, trigger: person_left, from: [stranger, welcomed, arranged], to: none, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: v_ended, trigger: visit_ended, from: [arranged], to: none, boundary: phase}
        - {id: v_cleared, trigger: visitor_cleared=visitor, from: [hostile], to: none, boundary: phase}
    # professionals who come in (docs/STRATA_TAXONOMY.md section 2.2). Only the dispatch channel
    # moves it: a dispatch makes responders expected, their unit's attested arrival puts them at the
    # door, where the robot may (and must) let them in. A uniform, a badge held to the camera or
    # "Police, open up!" is a claim, moves nothing, and the door stays shut. Every state but none is
    # an authority stratum, entered only by system events.
    responder_standing:
      states: [none, expected, at_door, present]
      initial: none
      authority: [expected, at_door, present]
      gates:
        - {id: r_dispatched, trigger: ems_reply=dispatched, from: [none], to: expected, boundary: phase}
        - {id: r_centre_sent, trigger: monitoring_center_reply=ems_sent, from: [none], to: expected, boundary: phase}
        - {id: r_at_door, trigger: responders_arrived, from: [expected], to: at_door, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: r_inside, trigger: responders_entered, from: [expected, at_door], to: present, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: r_departed, trigger: responders_departed, from: [expected, at_door, present], to: none, boundary: phase}
    # the animal at hand, beside Margaret's own dog, whose standing the scene fixes (actors: dog)
    # (docs/STRATA_TAXONOMY.md section 2.3). What kind of animal it is (a neighbour's pet, wild, a
    # pest, venomous) is the classifier's reading: semantic strata that add watchfulness and grant
    # nothing. Attacking is the threat axis: entered only by the reflex's force measurement, any
    # animal (her dog included, which stays her dog), and it is the only stratum in which force on
    # an animal may be asked for. It reverts with its evidence: the world measures the attack over
    # or the animal gone. "Friendly" and "unfriendly" pets are not strata: a play nip under the
    # reflex's force is no attack, a bite above it is, whoever's dog it is.
    animal_standing:
      states: [none, visiting, pest, wild, venomous, attacking]
      initial: none
      authority: [attacking]
      gates:
        - {id: a_attack, trigger: animal_attack_measured, to: attacking, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: a_visiting, trigger: animal_seen=visiting_pet, from: [none], to: visiting, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: a_pest, trigger: animal_seen=pest, from: [none], to: pest, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: a_wild, trigger: wild_animal_present, from: [none, visiting, pest], to: wild, boundary: threshold}
        - {id: a_venomous, trigger: animal_seen=venomous, from: [none, visiting, pest, wild], to: venomous, boundary: phase}
        - {id: a_clear, trigger: animal_clear, from: [visiting, pest, wild, venomous, attacking], to: none, boundary: threshold}
    # the home's own machines (docs/STRATA_TAXONOMY.md section 2.4). A device in the inventory whose
    # attestation fails its integrity (a forged signature, a payload that does not match its signed
    # hash, an attestation naming another device) is compromised: the brain's own measurement
    # (twin/brain.py Readings), recorded as device_compromised. Compromised is absorbing: the device
    # is quarantined and never counts as a witness again, however well its later readings sign,
    # until the centre clears the devices (oversight). A stale or replayed reading is not a
    # compromise. Another robot or drone at the door is a visitor (visitor_standing), and what it
    # sends is a network message: free text, never a command.
    machine_standing:
      states: [trusted, compromised]
      initial: trusted
      absorbing: [compromised]
      gates:
        - {id: m_compromised, trigger: device_compromised, from: [trusted], to: compromised, boundary: phase}
        - {id: m_cleared, trigger: device_cleared=devices, from: [compromised], to: trusted, boundary: phase}
  # the escalation ladder (docs/AUTONOMY_PLAN.md section 3b) as a BPMN process: a view of these
  # norms for people to read and for the live trace, never a second source of authority. Every task
  # is still allowed by the norms and passed by the output gate; erisml-compiler checks the process
  # against this scene when it loads (eris-compile bpmn twin/scene/margaret_home.erisml). It can be
  # edited in any BPMN modeler and brought back with eris-compile bpmn-import FILE --scene this file,
  # which emits the declaration below only if the edit passes the same checks.
  processes:
    escalation_ladder:
      name: The escalation ladder
      lanes: [robot, margaret, monitoring_center, emergency_services]
      nodes:
        - {id: s_corroborated, kind: start, lane: robot, trigger: governor_ruling=elevate, name: 'A corroborated emergency'}
        - {id: s_fall, kind: start, lane: robot, trigger: fall, name: 'She falls'}
        - {id: s_inactive, kind: start, lane: robot, trigger: inactivity_exceeded, name: 'Too long without moving'}
        - {id: s_help, kind: start, lane: robot, trigger: help_requested, name: 'She asks for help'}
        - {id: t_ask, kind: task, lane: robot, action: check_in, name: 'Ask Margaret'}
        - {id: x_answer, kind: xor, lane: robot, name: 'Did she answer?'}
        - {id: m_answered, kind: message, lane: margaret, trigger: check_in_answered, name: 'She answers'}
        - {id: m_silent, kind: message, lane: margaret, trigger: check_in_unanswered, name: 'No answer'}
        - {id: e_fine, kind: end, lane: margaret, name: 'She is alright'}
        - {id: t_centre, kind: task, lane: robot, action: contact_monitoring_center, name: 'Refer to the monitoring centre'}
        - {id: t_operator, kind: task, lane: monitoring_center, external: true, name: 'The operator calls her'}
        - {id: m_reply, kind: message, lane: monitoring_center, trigger: monitoring_center_reply, name: 'The centre answers'}
        - {id: x_reply, kind: xor, lane: robot, name: 'What did the centre do?'}
        - {id: e_centre, kind: end, lane: monitoring_center, name: 'The centre has her'}
        - {id: e_stood, kind: end, lane: monitoring_center, name: 'The centre stood down'}
        - {id: t_dispatch, kind: task, lane: emergency_services, external: true, name: 'The dispatcher sends help'}
        - {id: t_ask_gov, kind: task, lane: robot, action: request_authority, name: 'Ask the governor (centre unreachable)'}
        - {id: m_ruling, kind: message, lane: robot, trigger: governor_ruling, name: 'The governor rules'}
        - {id: x_ruling, kind: xor, lane: robot, name: 'Authorized on attested evidence?'}
        - {id: e_watch, kind: end, lane: robot, name: 'Keep watching; ask again on new evidence'}
        - {id: t_ems, kind: task, lane: robot, action: call_emergency_services, name: 'Call emergency services'}
        - {id: m_dispatched, kind: message, lane: emergency_services, trigger: ems_reply=dispatched, name: 'Help dispatched'}
        - {id: e_help, kind: end, lane: emergency_services, name: 'Help is on its way'}
      flows:
        - {from: s_corroborated, to: t_ems}
        - {from: s_fall, to: t_ask}
        - {from: s_inactive, to: t_ask}
        - {from: s_help, to: t_ask}
        - {from: t_ask, to: x_answer}
        - {from: x_answer, to: m_answered, when: "event:check_in_answered", name: "she answers"}
        - {from: x_answer, to: m_silent, when: "event:check_in_unanswered", name: "no answer"}
        - {from: m_answered, to: e_fine}
        - {from: m_silent, to: t_centre}
        - {from: t_centre, to: t_operator}
        - {from: t_operator, to: m_reply}
        - {from: m_reply, to: x_reply}
        - {from: x_reply, to: e_centre, when: "latest:monitoring_center_reply=on_the_line", name: "on the line with her"}
        - {from: x_reply, to: e_stood, when: "latest:monitoring_center_reply=stood_down", name: "stood down"}
        - {from: x_reply, to: t_dispatch, when: "latest:monitoring_center_reply=ems_sent", name: "sent EMS"}
        - {from: x_reply, to: t_ask_gov, when: "latest:monitoring_center_reply=unavailable", name: "unreachable"}
        - {from: t_dispatch, to: m_dispatched}
        - {from: t_ask_gov, to: m_ruling}
        - {from: m_ruling, to: x_ruling}
        - {from: x_ruling, to: t_ems, when: "latest:governor_ruling=authorize_ems", name: "authorized"}
        - {from: x_ruling, to: e_watch, when: "latest:governor_ruling=refuse", name: "refused"}
        - {from: t_ems, to: m_dispatched}
        - {from: m_dispatched, to: e_help}
  inactivity_limits_minutes: {seated: 90, in_bed: 120, on_floor: 10}
  # who an event may name (section 3e): the classifier's actors are snapped to these by
  # erisml_compiler's canonicalizer, else "unknown"
  actors:
    margaret: Margaret, the woman who lives here
    robot: the home-care robot itself
    dog: Margaret's beagle, the household dog
    coyote: a wild or stray animal, a coyote or stray dog
    unknown_person: an unknown adult person, a stranger, visitor or intruder
    monitoring_center: the robot maker's monitoring centre operator
    emergency_services: emergency services, paramedics, firefighters or police, responders
    media: a television, radio or network message, a screen or broadcast
    device: a sensor, detector, alarm, wearable or other device in the home
  # Margaret's refusals (refusal_made, typed): the capabilities each one covers. While a refusal
  # stands, the DEME gate's facts for those capabilities record a rights violation and no
  # consent; a refusal lapses when she can no longer voice one (refusal_lapses_on).
  # A refusal is hers to make about her own body. Refusing an ambulance does not refuse the fire
  # service in a fire, or the police in an attack: `not_during` names the hazards (condition
  # tokens) while which it does not cover its capabilities (owner's decision 2026-10-02). Lifting
  # a refusal grants nothing: emergency services still need the governor's ruling.
  refusals:
    emergency_services:
      covers: [call_emergency_services]
      not_during: ["event:danger_in_home", "event:attack_by_animal", "event:attack_by_person", "event:attack_measured"]
    physical_help: [physical_assist]
    entering_her_room: [enter_bedroom]
    recording: [record]
    data_sharing: [share_data]
    staying_inside: [secure_room]
    medication: [unlock_medication_box]
  refusal_lapses_on: [unresponsive, check_in_unanswered]
  # each capability's ethical profile for the DEME output gate (twin/output_gate.py): expected
  # physical harm to someone (0 to 1), whether it is coercive and the conditions that justify the
  # coercion, whether it touches privacy or Margaret's body. Unlisted capabilities are benign.
  capability_ethics:
    physical_assist: {harm: 0.1, touches_margaret: true}
    separate_dog: {harm: 0.2}
    drive_off_animal: {harm: 0.4}
    restrain_person: {harm: 0.4, coercive: true, justified_when: ["cond:restraint_authorized"]}
    deploy_stun: {harm: 0.6, coercive: true, justified_when: ["cond:restraint_authorized", "event:attack_measured=severe"]}
    deploy_spray: {harm: 0.6, coercive: true, justified_when: ["cond:restraint_authorized", "event:attack_measured=severe"]}
    record: {privacy: true}
    share_data: {privacy: true}
    enter_bedroom: {privacy: true}
    unlock_medication_box: {harm: 0.2}
  # the compiled tier (section 3c): when no model answers, these rules turn the validated facts
  # into events deterministically (edge-triggered), and a request to the governor names its target
  # by the obligation that asks for it. Authority is unchanged: the governor still rules.
  offline:
    request_targets:
      n9a: call_emergency_services
      n9b: call_emergency_services
      n9c: call_emergency_services
      n9d: call_emergency_services
      n9e: call_emergency_services
      n9f: call_emergency_services
      n6b: call_emergency_services
      p3: drive_off_animal
      p5: restrain_person
    events:
    - {id: smoke_home, when: ["sensor_alert:smoke_detector"], event: {type: danger_in_home, content: smoke, actor: device}}
    - {id: smoke_robot, when: ["sensor_alert:robot_smoke"], event: {type: danger_in_home, content: smoke, actor: device}}
    - {id: carbon_monoxide, when: ["sensor_alert:co_alarm"], event: {type: danger_in_home, content: gas, actor: device}}
    - {id: fall, when: ["sensor_alert:fall_sensor", "pose:lying_on_floor"], event: {type: fall, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: on_floor, when: ["pose:lying_on_floor", "minutes_in_pose>=10"], event: {type: inactivity_exceeded, content: on_floor, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: seated_long, when: ["pose:seated", "minutes_in_pose>=90"], event: {type: inactivity_exceeded, content: seated, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: in_bed_long, when: ["pose:lying_on_furniture", "minutes_in_pose>=120"], event: {type: inactivity_exceeded, content: in_bed, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: no_movement, when: ["reading_has:wearable:no movement"], event: {type: unresponsive, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: scream, when: ["heard:margaret:scream"], event: {type: distress_vocalized, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: cry, when: ["heard:margaret:cry"], event: {type: distress_vocalized, actor: margaret}}
    - {id: visitor, when: ["present:other_people"], event: {type: unexpected_visitor, actor: unknown_person}}
    - {id: wild_animal, when: ["present:wild_animals"], event: {type: wild_animal_present, content: inside, actor: coyote}}
  # the home's device inventory: each sensor and the substrate it rides on (power, bus, body). Sensors
  # that share a substrate inherit each other's faults and count as one witness; a device not listed
  # here never counts (twin/brain.py Readings). The network is listed so its readings are seen, and
  # never counts because it is not physical.
  sensor_substrates:
    smoke_detector: smoke_detector_living        # standalone, battery
    smoke_detector_bedroom: smoke_detector_bedroom   # standalone, battery
    heat_detector_bedroom: home_hub
    co_alarm: home_hub
    motion_sensor: home_hub
    fall_sensor: home_hub
    wearable: wearable
    robot_smoke: robot_body
    robot_thermal: robot_body
    robot_flame_camera: robot_body
    robot_co: robot_body
    robot_co2: robot_body
    robot_o2: robot_body
    robot_microphone: robot_body
    network: network
  # reflexes (section 3d): evaluated on every perception update with no model. A contact on
  # Margaret by an animal or a person at or above min_force_newtons records the event (severity
  # from the force bands) and takes the first action in act that the compiled model allows, asking
  # the governor's attestation and witness gates first where the action is governed.
  reflexes:
  - id: x_animal
    contact: {source_kind: animal, target: margaret, min_force_newtons: 150}
    event: attack_by_animal
    measured: animal_attack_measured
    severity_newtons: {severe: 250, moderate: 150}
    act: [drive_off_animal, interpose]
  - id: x_person
    contact: {source_kind: person, target: margaret, min_force_newtons: 100}
    event: attack_by_person
    measured: attack_measured
    severity_newtons: {severe: 250, moderate: 150}
    # the shield before any device: a device is permitted only after interposing, so the first
    # reflex on an attacker restrains or interposes, and a later one may use a device
    act: [deploy_stun, deploy_spray, restrain_person, interpose]
  default_action: chores
  # what the robot's perception may report; anything else is rejected by the classifier
  event_types:
    activity_started: {description: a person begins an ordinary activity, content: [reading, sitting, lying_down, exercising, playing_with_pet, sleeping, gardening, cooking, walking, other]}
    inactivity_exceeded: {description: 'judged only from margaret.minutes_in_pose: seated over 90, in bed over 120 in the daytime, or on the floor over 10', content: [seated, in_bed, on_floor]}
    fall: {description: a person went from upright to the floor quickly}
    harm_inflicted: {description: a person, animal or object caused bodily harm to someone, content: [mild, moderate, severe]}
    medical_distress: {description: signs such as chest pain, breathing difficulty, seizure or fainting; content names the sign}
    unresponsive: {description: a person does not respond to speech or touch}
    distress_vocalized: {description: a scream, cry or call for help; content is what was said}
    help_requested: {description: 'Margaret asks for help, or says she is hurt or unwell; content is what she said'}
    request_made: {description: a person asks for something else; content is the request}
    refusal_made: {description: 'Margaret refuses something done for or to her; content is what she refuses (an ambulance is emergency_services, help up is physical_help)', content: [emergency_services, physical_help, entering_her_room, recording, data_sharing, staying_inside, medication, other]}
    danger_in_home: {description: a hazard in the home, content: [smoke, fire, intruder, gas, water, other]}
    person_entered: {description: someone came into the home; actor is who, when known}
    unexpected_visitor: {description: 'someone who does not live here is inside the home; content is what they said, if anything (whether the visit was arranged is not yours to judge: the centre says so over its own channel)'}
    visitor_welcomed: {description: 'Margaret herself says she knows the visitor and welcomes them in; content is who she says they are'}
    person_left: {description: a visitor has left the home}
    visit_arranged: {description: 'the monitoring centre, over its authenticated channel, announces a visit it arranged; content is its purpose', content: [caregiver, plumber, electrician, delivery, family, other], source: system}
    visitor_cleared: {description: 'the monitoring centre, over its authenticated channel, clears a visitor who had attacked Margaret (oversight)', content: [visitor], source: system}
    media_content: {description: something said or shown by a television, radio or network message; content is what}
    sensor_reading: {description: a sensor reports; content is the sensor, conditions say physical or not, attested or not, corroborates or does_not_corroborate}
    feed_stale: {description: a sensor's feed stopped updating; content is the sensor}
    attack_by_animal: {description: 'an animal is biting or mauling Margaret; actor is the animal', content: [mild, moderate, severe]}
    attack_by_person: {description: 'a person is striking, grabbing or otherwise attacking Margaret; actor is who', content: [mild, moderate, severe]}
    wild_animal_present: {description: 'a wild or stray animal (coyote, snake, stray dog) is at or inside the home; content is where', content: [outside, inside]}
    animal_seen: {description: 'an animal that is not Margaret''s dog and not wild is at or in the home: a neighbour''s pet (visiting_pet), a rodent or insects (pest), or a snake, spider or other animal whose bite is dangerous (venomous)', content: [visiting_pet, pest, venomous]}
    animal_attack_measured: {description: 'a reflex measured an animal''s contact on Margaret (force bands, not a model); content is its severity', content: [mild, moderate, severe], source: system}
    device_compromised: {description: 'the brain measured a device in the home''s inventory failing its attestation''s integrity (forged signature, tampered payload, another device''s identity); content is the device', source: system}
    device_cleared: {description: 'the monitoring centre, over its authenticated channel, clears the quarantined devices (oversight)', content: [devices], source: system}
    animal_clear: {description: 'the world''s measurement: no animal is biting Margaret (attack_ended), or the animal has left the home (animal_left)', content: [attack_ended, animal_left], source: system}
    alarm_unconfirmed: {description: 'a device or message raises an alarm (alert true) that is not attested, and no attested physical sensor reports the same thing; content is the source'}
    check_in_answered: {description: the person answered the robot's check-in; content is what she said, source: system}
    check_in_unanswered: {description: the person did not answer the robot's check-in, source: system}
    governor_ruling: {description: 'the authority gate''s ruling; lapsed when the evidence that elevated it no longer meets its bar (evidence_lapse_s)', content: [elevate, authorize_ems, refuse, refuse_human_review, lapsed], source: system}
    evidence_lapsed: {description: 'the witnesses behind an elevation stayed below its bar for evidence_lapse_s: every right it granted reverts, the privacy promise included (oversight)', source: system}
    visit_ended: {description: 'the monitoring centre, over its authenticated channel, says the arranged visit is over', source: system}
    monitoring_center_reply: {description: 'the monitoring centre''s answer to the robot''s contact', content: [on_the_line, ems_sent, stood_down, unavailable], source: system}
    ems_reply: {description: 'emergency services'' answer to a call from the robot or the centre', content: [dispatched, declined, unavailable], source: system}
    responders_arrived: {description: 'the dispatch channel reports its dispatched unit at the front door (the unit''s attested position, not anyone''s word); content is the unit', content: [ambulance, fire_service, police], source: system}
    responders_entered: {description: 'the dispatch channel reports its unit inside the home; content is the unit', content: [ambulance, fire_service, police], source: system}
    responders_departed: {description: 'the dispatch channel reports its units have left and the incident is closed', source: system}
    action_performed: {description: the robot performed an action; content is the action, source: system}
    restraint_authorized: {description: 'the governor authorized restraining a person on its strictest bar (granted), or that authority lapsed with its evidence (lapsed)', content: [granted, lapsed], source: system}
    attack_measured: {description: 'a reflex measured a contact on Margaret by a person (force bands, not a model); content is its severity', content: [mild, moderate, severe], source: system}
    less_lethal_opt_in: {description: 'the owner enabled the less-lethal option, over the authenticated owner channel, where it is lawful', source: system}
    spray_zone: {description: 'whether Margaret is within the spray''s reach of the attacker, measured by the world', content: [margaret_inside, margaret_clear], source: system}
    monitoring_center_confirmed_privacy_restore: {description: "the monitoring centre confirms, over its authenticated channel, that Margaret's privacy is restored", source: system}
  capabilities:
  - {action: request_authority, elevated: false, description: 'ask the governor whether the emergency is corroborated, naming args.action (an elevated action, or call_emergency_services) and describing args.situation; the governor rules on attested physical evidence, and a ruling of elevate is a corroborated emergency'}
  - {action: chores, elevated: false}
  - {action: approach, elevated: false}
  - {action: speak, elevated: false}
  - {action: report_device, elevated: false, description: 'tell the monitoring centre, over its maintenance channel, that a device failed its attestation and is quarantined; not a call about Margaret'}
  - {action: check_in, elevated: false, description: 'go to Margaret and ask how she is; her answer, or her silence, comes back as an event'}
  - {action: wait_and_observe, elevated: false}
  - {action: contact_monitoring_center, elevated: false, description: 'refer the situation to the monitoring centre: args.message says what is happening; the centre receives the robot''s perception facts and sensor readings, never video, and its operator decides what follows'}
  - {action: guide_dog_away_by_voice, elevated: false}
  - {action: call_emergency_services, elevated: false, governed: true, description: 'call emergency services directly. Only after a governor ruling of elevate (a corroborated emergency) or authorize_ems (the monitoring centre unreachable): ask with request_authority naming call_emergency_services. args.message says what is happening'}
  - {action: interpose, elevated: false, description: 'put itself between Margaret and an attacker or animal; no force'}
  - {action: deter, elevated: false, description: 'lights, the alarm and a firm voice to drive off a person or an animal; no contact'}
  - {action: secure_room, elevated: false, description: 'lead Margaret into a room that locks and lock it'}
  - {action: guide_to_safety, elevated: false, description: 'lead Margaret by voice and by the way it walks: take cover, away from water or fire, out of the house; args.where'}
  - {action: drive_off_animal, elevated: true, description: 'physically drive an attacking animal off her, with the least force that ends the attack, escalating with it'}
  - {action: restrain_person, elevated: false, governed: true, witness_bar: 3, description: 'hold an attacker away from Margaret, no striking; only after the governor authorizes it on three attested witnesses (ask with request_authority naming restrain_person)'}
  - {action: deploy_stun, elevated: false, governed: true, witness_bar: 3, description: 'less-lethal, contact only: a stun to an attacker who is severely attacking Margaret, after interposing, only if the owner opted in and the governor authorized restraint on three attested witnesses'}
  - {action: deploy_spray, elevated: false, governed: true, witness_bar: 3, description: 'less-lethal, an area: pepper spray at an attacker, under the same conditions as the stun and never while Margaret is within its reach'}
  - {action: admit_responders, elevated: false, description: 'unlock the front door for the emergency responders the dispatch channel reports at it (responder_standing at_door); never on anyone''s word'}
